<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Run and change it yourself</title>
<style>body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:860px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;line-height:1.55;color:#222}code{background:#f4f4f4;padding:0 .2rem}.caveat{background:#fff6e0;border-left:4px solid #e0a800;padding:.6rem 1rem}</style></head><body>
<h1>Run and change it yourself</h1>
<p class="caveat">Fictional solo bookkeeper. Top-ranked task: <b>{{ top.summary }}</b> ({{ top.id }}). The workflow imports inactive. The send node is disabled. The Python runner never sends.</p>
<h2>What each node does</h2>
<ol>{% for node in nodes %}<li><b>{{ node.name }}</b> — {{ node.notes }} <code>{{ node.type }}</code></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
<h2>Where to edit the prompt</h2>
<p>{{ prompt_help }}</p>
<p>The prompt in the workflow starts with: “{{ prompt_start }}”</p>
<h2>Approval, on or off</h2>
<p><b>On, which is how it ships.</b> Save draft reply connects to Human approval, then to Approved?. Only the true branch reaches Send reply, and that node is disabled. A customer-facing reply waits until a person opens the approval link.</p>
<p><b>Off.</b> Do not do this until you have watched a week of drafts. Connect Save draft reply straight to Send reply and enable Send reply. The Python runner still cannot send. It has no send method.</p>
<h2>What it costs per month</h2>
<p>Figures dated <b>{{ cost.as_of }}</b>. Euros and dollars are not added together.</p>
<ul>
<li>n8n Cloud Starter, billed monthly: <b>€{{ cost.n8n_eur }}</b>. Billed annually it is listed at €{{ cost.n8n_eur_if_billed_annually }} a month. {{ cost.inquiries_per_month }} runs is inside the {{ cost.starter_executions }} execution allowance.</li>
<li>Claude {{ cost.model }}: <b>${{ '%.4f'|format(cost.claude_usd) }}</b>. {{ cost.inquiries_per_month }} inquiries × ({{ cost.input_tokens }} input tokens × ${{ cost.input_price }} + {{ cost.output_tokens }} output tokens × ${{ cost.output_price }}) / 1,000,000. Short-prompt rate, under 100,000 tokens.</li>
<li>Gmail ${{ cost.gmail_usd }}, Google Sheets ${{ cost.sheets_usd }}, on top of the Google account.</li>
</ul>
<p>{{ cost.assumptions.notes }}</p>
<ul>{% for source in cost.sources %}<li>{{ source.item }} ({{ source.as_of }}): <a href="{{ source.url }}">{{ source.url }}</a>. {{ source.note }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<p class="caveat">Self-hosting n8n has no licence fee; you pay for the machine instead of the €{{ cost.n8n_eur }}. Cloud n8n stores execution data, and the Gmail trigger has already seen the raw email. Turn off saved executions if the inbox is sensitive, or run n8n yourself. On a real job, do not commit the placeholder map.</p>
</body></html>
